{
  "root": "Daily",
  "covers": "MRefreshControl: a region of a fixed height with the label, the refresh button and the status line over content that scrolls; the button runs refresh, a refresh that succeeds shows the success label and one that throws shows the error label and the retry label on the button, and onStateChange reports each state; a disabled control does not refresh; NativeScript keeps both titles in its view tree, so its expectations name the label twice",
  "steps": [
    {
      "expect": [
        "Edition 1",
        "A different way to start",
        "Small things, noticed",
        "Make time for a detour",
        "Morning edition",
        "Refresh",
        "Last state: idle"
